Artifact: postgresql-15.18-pgrestore.dump
SHA-256: b01eca32413c8d3ee6e7ac59c141a36412f8c003d580dd898e489ac8e4cc9fbb
Generated: 2026-07-28
Generator: pg_dump (PostgreSQL) 15.18 (Homebrew)
Archive format: PostgreSQL custom archive 1.14

Source: postgresql-18.4-plain-dump.sql
Source SHA-256: 104e92ad8657d8de41925383d9c468abea5002678cf5cb269a65467cbb0c89e5

The source fixture was loaded into a vanilla PostgreSQL 15.18 cluster after
removing PostgreSQL 18's two psql-only \restrict/\unrestrict guard lines and
the PostgreSQL-18-only `SET transaction_timeout = 0` line. No SQL object or
COPY data was otherwise changed. The fixture objects were reassigned to a
locally created `postgres` role so the archive retains and tests owner
statements, then generated with:

    pg_dump --format=custom --file=postgresql-15.18-pgrestore.dump postgres

The archive was listed with PostgreSQL 15.18 pg_restore and restored with
PostgreSQL 18.4 pg_restore before its checksum was recorded above.
